Title: NIGHT SHIFT
Author: Sample

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S HOSPITAL - WAITING ROOM - NIGHT

Rain hammers the window. A vending machine hums. MARA DELACROIX, 40s, still
in a soaked PARAMEDIC JACKET, holds a paper CUP of coffee she has not touched.

Across from her, a boy of nine, ELIOT, folds and refolds a hospital GOWN.

MARA
You should sleep.

ELIOT
I'm not tired.

MARA
That's not what I asked.

Eliot looks at the double DOORS. They stay shut.

ELIOT
Is she going to die?

Mara sets the cup down. Very carefully.

MARA
I don't know.

CUT TO:

EXT. HOSPITAL LOADING BAY - NIGHT

Rain. An AMBULANCE idles, its LIGHT BAR throwing red across the wet concrete.
DR. YUSUF OKONKWO, 50s, smokes a CIGARETTE he clearly doesn't want.

A second AMBULANCE screams in. PARAMEDICS pour out with a GURNEY. A CROWD of
night staff swells around the doors. Chaos.

YUSUF
Talk to me.

PARAMEDIC
Sixty-one, male, cardiac. Down eleven minutes.

They crash through the doors.

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S HOSPITAL - CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS

The GURNEY rockets past. Fluorescent LIGHTS strobe overhead.

Mara stands as it passes. She sees the man's face. She knows him.

MARA
No. No, no, no --

She runs.

INT. ST. BRENDAN'S HOSPITAL - TRAUMA BAY - CONTINUOUS

Controlled violence. A DEFIBRILLATOR whines up. BLOOD on the floor. Yusuf
works the chest. A MONITOR flatlines.

YUSUF
Charging. Clear.

The body arches. Nothing.

YUSUF (CONT'D)
Again.

Through the window, Mara watches. Eliot appears beside her, silent.

EXT. ST. BRENDAN'S HOSPITAL - ROOF - DAWN

Grey light. The rain has stopped. Mara sits on the ledge, the PARAMEDIC JACKET
around Eliot's shoulders now. The city exhales below them.

ELIOT
You knew him.

MARA
A long time ago.

They watch the sun come up over the water towers.

FADE OUT.
